Description: compositor: A mirror of stereo eyes in another colour space converts them on the copy
 .
 An output that replicates one with stereo eyes copied only when both blend in the
 same colour space (the A10's laptop panel and TV never did: 6989 "another colour
 space" refusals in a run, so the TV painted the scene again, GPU 97%). When they
 differ, the replica now draws the eyes into its own with the pair's conversion table
 (one draw, scaled and converted at once, the shader of the scene pass) instead of
 the plain blit, when the table gives what painting again would give; HDR content on
 screen, an ICC profile and the cases of the earlier commit stay on the old path with
 the reason logged. KWIN_STEREO_REPLICA_COPY=0 still keeps the old path everywhere.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: https://invent.kde.org/danielcamposramos/kwin/-/commit/3d8faa079732a3ca10c44423057cf3f034b72f14
Forwarded: no
